// expect: 7
// A DECLARED anonymous rest with no closed partner in the body. The only
// thing that ever narrows `u` is another open row, so the residual `pick`
// carries is a union of two partial sets and nothing is known past it.
// The projection must say so: an empty remainder from a closed partner is
// a proof, an empty remainder from two partial sets is a guess, and they
// rendered identically before the tail carried what its writer knew.
//
// The 7 is the wrong-slot class itself, measured and pinned rather than
// asserted: `zeta` is index 0 of the KNOWN set and index 1 of the real
// record, so this answers `alpha`. The fixture holds the CURRENT answer so
// the day it changes is a day someone chose
// (`Hβ.lower.open-row-field-offset-from-known-set`).
fn pick(u: {zeta: Int, ...}) = u.zeta
fn main(q) = pick({alpha: 7, zeta: 9})
